              <span id="res-buffer" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-mono text-amber-400">+49.5%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <script is:inline>
          function updateFundingCalc() {
            var capital = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calc-capital').value) || 10000;
            var ratePct = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calc-rate').value) || 0.01;
            var leverage = parseFloat(document.getElementById('calc-leverage').value) || 2;

            var rDecimal = ratePct / 100;
            var apr = rDecimal * 3 * 365 * 100;
            var apy = (Math.pow(1 + rDecimal, 1095) - 1) * 100;

            // Half capital allocated to short perp
            var annualDollars = capital * (apr / 100);
            var bufferPct = (1 / leverage - 0.005) * 100;

            document.getElementById('res-apy').textContent = apr.toFixed(1) + '% / ' + apy.toFixed(1) + '%';
            document.getElementById('res-yield').textContent = '$' + Math.round(annualDollars).toLocaleString() + ' / yr';
            document.getElementById('res-buffer').textContent = '+' + bufferPct.toFixed(1) + '%';
          }

          document.getElementById('calc-capital').addEventListener('input', updateFundingCalc);
          document.getElementById('calc-rate').addEventListener('input', updateFundingCalc);
          document.getElementById('calc-leverage').addEventListener('change', updateFundingCalc);
        </script>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Operational Risk Guardrails -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono">6.</span> Institutional Execution Protocol &amp; Risk Guardrails
        </h2>
        <p>
          Executing multi-million dollar basis arbitrage mandates strict algorithmic guardrails:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-3 text-slate-200">
          <li><strong>Dynamic Collateral Sweeping:</strong> As spot assets appreciate, unrealized spot profits should be periodically re-margined into the derivative exchange or used as cross-collateral to push liquidation thresholds higher.</li>
          <li><strong>Execution Slippage &amp; Fee Drag:</strong> Trading desks must account for maker/taker fee tiers (e.g., 0.02% maker, 0.05% taker). Incurring a 0.10% round-trip trading fee consumes nearly 3 days of baseline funding income. Always use passive post-only limit orders.</li>
          <li><strong>Negative Rate Unwind Thresholds:</strong> Programmatic stop-losses must trigger if the 72-hour exponential moving average of the funding rate drops below -0.005%, preventing prolonged capital bleed during prolonged bear capitulation events.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

